    <string name="help_dialog_title">Help &amp; Credits</string>
    <string name="help_dialog_message">UAE4ARM is an Amiga emulator for Android.

<b>AGS (Amiga Game Selector)</b>
To use AGS, you need a .uae configuration file with all drives listed (DF0:, HD0:, etc.) pointing to your AGS folder structure. The emulator will boot directly into the AGS menu where you can browse and launch games.

<b>On-Screen Controls</b>
Open the controller mapping screen (gamepad icon) to choose an on-screen controller (None, Joystick, or CD32 Pad). The virtual keyboard can be toggled with the pencil icon.

<b>External Controller Mapping</b>
Tap the gamepad icon to open the controller mapping screen. Tap a CD32 button on the pad graphic, then press a physical button on your controller to assign it. Extra buttons (Select, L2, R2, L3, R3) can be mapped to Amiga keyboard keys.

<b>Credits</b>
AGS (Amiga Game Selector) created by Paul Vince — thank you for this amazing contribution to the Amiga community.

Based on UAE/WinUAE by Bernd Schmidt, Toni Wilen, and many contributors.
Upstream Copperline core derived from Amiberry.
SDL by Sam Lantinga and contributors.</string>
